  evidence:
  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH
    source: MIM curation (#114)
    notes: 'ATCC Wolfe''s mineral mix is a named, recurring multi-component preparation
      (46 media). Searched CHEBI, NCIT, MeSH, FOODON and ENVO by label and synonym
      with normalisation: no term denotes it, and none could -- it is a lab preparation
      rather than a substance. Takes the STOCK_SOLUTION convention used by the existing
      mapped records: a kgmicrobe.ingredient: mint, with no parent because a multi-component
      mix does not narrow to any single compound (#114).'
